extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 74-76 (cache p075-p077, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order, with the stat block on cache p077 checked against a render. The entry heading Roadganger O.C.C. is at the foot of printed 74; the stat block, headed Roadganger NPC Villain & Optional Player Character (also known as Desert Riders), starts on printed 75 and fills printed 76. || HEADING: the book heads the class an NPC villain and optional player character; it is imported as playable and tagged evil on that heading (survey decision 1, 2026-10-01), although the alignment line is Any. It is listed under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56, which has no men-at-arms heading; occ_group men-of-arms is a reading of the class as a warrior. The class prints its own Base S.D.C., so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the Jackaroo, Roadganger & Sportsman ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || S.D.C.: Base S.D.C. 4D6 is sdc_base; the O.C.C. bonus of +1D4x10 physical S.D.C. is a pool bonus (the text layer prints +lD4xlO; the render shows +1D4x10). || BONUSES: +1 initiative at levels 1, 3, 5, 6, 8, 10 and 12 stored as 1 plus six at_level entries; +1 strike, +1 pull punch, +2 roll, +4 vs Horror Factor stored. The +1 melee attack when riding a vehicle and shooting from a moving vehicle without penalty are conditional and are a special_abilities entry. || SKILLS: Speak English 80% is stored as Language: Australian English at 80 with the catalog per-level rate. Pilot: Motorcycle or (+20%) is printed with the second option missing; Motorcycles & Snowmobiles is stored alone. Pilot: Automobile or Hover Vehicle is a choice between Automobile and Hover Craft (ground). Outback Combat Driving is the catalog row Combat Driving. W.P. Archery & Targeting is stored as the two catalog rows. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Assassin each cost one other skill. || RELATED: three Physical, two Military or Espionage and three others are stored as count 8 with two floors. The +5% printed for the three Physical picks is stored as the Physical category bonus, so a fourth Physical pick also gets it. Pilot except Robot Elite and boats is stored as the Robot Combat Elite rows, the five Boat rows and the two Military boat rows. Science Math only is read as both Mathematics rows. Cowboy is printed None and left out; the book lists no Horsemanship category. || MONEY: 1D4x100 in cash stored (printed lD4x$100); the 2D6x100 of saleable or tradeable items is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: camp stove, a basic kit bag (crude cutlery, a half empty box of matches, bandages, odds and ends) and the basic tools carried in the vehicle have no row. The armor choice offers this book''s five homespun M.D.C. rows. The vehicle (motorcycle, pickup truck or jeep-type vehicle with a 20,000 dollar improvement budget that cannot be kept as cash) is in GM Notes. || NOT STORED: gang sizes (3-12 up to several hundred) and the 15-20% who ride Giant Kang are background."
